# LINK_DRIP_API_KEY="" # Your LinkDrip API key
# LINK_DRIP_API_ENDPOINT="https://api.linkdrip.com/v1/" # Your self-hosted LinkDrip API endpoint
# LINK_DRIP_SHORT_LINK_DOMAIN="dripl.ink" # Your self-hosted LinkDrip domain

# === Deployment identity (leave unset for a single-host install)
## Where your Terms and Privacy pages live, if they are not served by this app.
#LEGAL_URL="https://example.com"
## Who reviews new agency signups. Unset means nobody is notified.
#AGENCY_NOTIFICATION_EMAIL=""
## Your own affiliate programme, if you run one. Unset hides the menu entry.
#AFFILIATE_URL=""
## Inbox behind Help -> Contact support and Help -> Report a bug. Unlike the
## rest of this block it has a default (support@postqueen.ai), because those two
## rows always render: Chatbase and Sentry below are both optional, and an
## install with neither still has to leave a way to reach a human. Set it to
## your own address, or your users' bug reports come to us.
#SUPPORT_EMAIL="support@postqueen.ai"
## Your release notes, if you publish any. Unset hides the Help menu entry.
#CHANGELOG_URL=""
## Your community or chat invite. Unset hides the Help menu entry.
#COMMUNITY_URL=""
## Your own Chrome Web Store listing, if you publish a build of the extension.
## Unset hides the install prompts — the upstream build only talks to its own
## domain, so pointing your users at it would hand them something that cannot work.
#EXTENSION_STORE_URL=""
## Your own onboarding/tutorial video. Unset hides the player rather than
## showing your users somebody else's video.
#ONBOARDING_VIDEO_URL=""
## Where your source code is published. AGPL asks you to offer the source of
## *your* modified version, so this should point at your fork, not upstream.
## Unset drops the link from the FAQ.
#REPOSITORY_URL=""
## Your MCP server, if you run one. Shown in the Connections catalog's code
## samples; unset leaves those samples with an empty host.
#MCP_URL=""
## The address the MCP server advertises for its own OAuth endpoints. Only set
## this when clients must reach the backend on a different host than
## NEXT_PUBLIC_BACKEND_URL, which is what it falls back to.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_OVERRIDE_BACKEND_URL=""
## Domain-verification string for publishing an OpenAI app. When set, the MCP
## server echoes it back on the challenge route. Nothing else reads it.
#OPENAI_APP_CHALLANGE=""
## Version shown next to the logo and in the Help menu. Normally injected at
## build time; unset falls back to a hardcoded string that will drift.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=""
## Stripe coupon offered in the cancel flow. Unset means the retention offer is
## never shown and cancelling goes straight through.
#STRIPE_DISCOUNT_ID=""
## Google Ads conversion label fired when a trial starts. Needs
## NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID as well.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_TRACKING_TRIAL=""
## Sentry Spotlight, a local debug UI. Compared to the exact string "1".
#SENTRY_SPOTLIGHT="1"
## Chatbase support widget. The bot must be one you own: its agent can call the
## refund tool, which acts on the signed-in user's own subscription. The widget
## only loads when BOTH are set.
#CHATBASE_BOT_ID=""
#CHATBASE_TOKEN=""

# === Analytics (each loads only when its own key is set)
## Dub.co click tracking. Loads a third-party script and sets cookies, so it
## stays off until you configure it.
#DUB_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
## Meta pixel. When set, `pnpm install` downloads fbevents.js into
## apps/frontend/public/f.js; unset, nothing is downloaded and no pixel loads.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_FACEBOOK_PIXEL=""
## Server-side companion to the pixel (Conversions API). Needs the pixel id
## above as well; on its own it sends nothing.
#FACEBOOK_PIXEL_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
## PostHog. Both are needed — the key alone loads nothing.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=""
#NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST="https://eu.i.posthog.com"
## Google Tag Manager / Google Ads. Unset means the container never loads.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=""
## Datafast. The website id loads the script; the API key is what lets the
## backend attribute a signup to a visitor. Either can be set without the other.
#DATAFAST_WEBSITE_ID=""
#DATAFAST_API_KEY=""
## Sentry. Unset means the SDK is never initialised, on the server or in the
## browser — which is the case the SUPPORT_EMAIL note above is about.
#NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=""

# Provider visibility / migration
# HIDDEN_PROVIDERS="tiktok" # comma-separated identifiers hidden from the add-channel screen
# MIGRATE_PROVIDERS="tiktok:tiktok-business" # comma-separated "old:new" pairs, a reconnect of "old" goes through "new" and the channel is migrated in place
